        "question": {
          ":question/id": "c870678d-a04a-579a-ba28-d8b7f14642d2",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Suppose $|\\mathbf{v}|=9 \\sqrt{3}$ and the angle between nonzero vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ is $\\theta=\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}$. Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{v}$ onto $\\mathbf{u}$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{comp}_{\\mathbf{u}}\\mathbf{v}=$\n{{field-1}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cosine of the included angle to find the signed scalar projection.\n\nWe project $\\mathbf{v}$, so we use $|\\mathbf{v}|=9 \\sqrt{3}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{comp}_{\\mathbf{u}}\\mathbf{v} &=|\\mathbf{v}|\\cos\\theta \\\\\n&=9 \\sqrt{3}\\cos\\left(\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\\n&=9 \\sqrt{3}\\cdot\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scalar projection is negative because the included angle is obtuse.",
